# Add server actions with Datastar

Rocci uses Datastar as a transport for server-rendered updates. The browser
declares an action, the Roc handler changes state, and the response replaces a
targeted HTML fragment.

This guide sketches the counter included in `examples/counter`.

## Declare application state

```rocci
import pf.Sqlite

@context { db : Sqlite.Db }

@init {
    db = Sqlite.open!(Sqlite.default_config(Path.utf8("./counter.db")))?
    { db: db }
}
```

`@context` defines the state record used by generated handlers. `@init` creates
that state once when the standalone app starts.

## Serve the document

```rocci
@on:get("/") = |{ db }| {
    count = read_count!(db)?
    counterPage({ count })
}
```

GET handlers return complete HTML documents. Rocci generates a basic-webserver
dispatcher around the authored function.

## Return a targeted patch

```rocci
@on:post("/actions/counter/increment") = |{ db }| {
    count = increment_count!(db)?
    counterCard({ count })
}

@component CounterCard = |{ count }|
    <section id="counter">
        <p>Shared count</p>
        <output>{count.to_str()}</output>
    </section>
```

Non-GET handlers return one-shot `datastar-patch-elements` events. The stable
`id` lets Datastar target the existing fragment.

## Trigger the action

```rocci
<button data-on:click=@post("/actions/counter/increment")>
    Increment
</button>
```

The `@post` attribute form is Rocci syntax. Rocci injects the Datastar import
and produces the client expression. Its argument is Roc and therefore uses
double-quoted Roc strings.

> A quoted value such as `data-on:click="@post('/actions/x')"` stays an opaque
> Datastar expression. Use the unquoted Rocci action form when the URL depends
> on Roc values or when you want compiler help.

## Choose route conventions

| Response | Suggested route | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| HTML document | Resource path | `GET /todos` |
| HTML or SSE patch | `/actions/...` | `POST /actions/todos/add` |
| JSON API | `/api/...` | `POST /api/direction` |
| Long-lived SSE | `/sse` | `GET /sse` in an authored `main.roc` |

## Run the complete example

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/counter/Counter.rocci
```

Increment the counter in two browser windows to verify that SQLite-backed
state is shared. See [the rendering model](/docs/concepts/rendering-model/) for the
boundary between documents, patches, and client behavior.
